                     <msItem>
                        <title>Misc. historica</title>
                        <note>Fol. 66 is an isolated parchment folio giving a list of abbots of
                           Westminster up to George Norwych (1463–69).</note>
                     </msItem>
                  </msContents>
                  <history>
                     <origin>
                        <origDate when-custom="14XX" notBefore="1400" notAfter="1499"
                           calendar="#gregorian">s. xv</origDate>
                     </origin>
                     <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_579">Westminster, Middlesex.
                           Benedictine abbey of St Peter</orgName>
                        <p><q>Sequitur extraccio et compilacio tocius operis sequentis per fratrem
                              Ricardum quondam monachum ecclesie Westm. a.d. mcccclo</q> (top of
                           first page of first work, fol. 16r, s. xv).<q>Compilacio per fratrem
                                 <persName>[Ricardum Spor]ley</persName> monach[um Westm'] collecta
                              ex . . .</q> (top of first page of second work, fol. 34r, s. xv). The
                           heading on fol. 34 in which the hand of the collector has been inserted
                           by a contemporary or the same hand is partly illegible: parts of words in
                           brackets are supplied in a post-medieval hand.</p>
                        <p>
                           <q>Oro orate pro me <persName>Ihone felix</persName> huius sancti cenobii
                              Westm' monacho</q> (fol. 65, in a humanist script which also writes
                           fol. 64v-65). For Sporley and Felix (1524–25), see E. Pearce,
                              <title>Monks of Westminster</title> (Cambridge,
                        1916).</p></provenance>
                  </history>
